                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Bahá'í: Manifestation of God in Progressive Revelation", body: "In the Bahá'í Faith, Jesus is honored as a \"Manifestation of God\" — a divine messenger who reveals God's will to humanity. Bahá'ís place Jesus in a line of major figures: Abraham, Moses, Krishna, Buddha, Zoroaster, Muhammad, and culminating with Bahá'u'lláh in the 19th century.\n\nJesus is not viewed as just a teacher, but also not as God incarnate in the Trinitarian sense. Instead, Bahá'í thought emphasizes progressive revelation — God sends messengers across history, each bringing guidance suited to their time, all pointing to the same ultimate God.\n\nBahá'ís revere the Gospels and accept many core elements of Jesus's story — his moral authority, his suffering, and the power of his message. But they interpret certain doctrines differently, especially resurrection (seen as spiritually real — the triumph of Jesus's cause — rather than primarily physical).\n\nThe \"return of Christ\" is understood as the appearance of a new messenger carrying the same divine authority — like a new sunrise, not the old sun coming back.\n\nThis view tries to preserve Jesus's greatness while building bridges between religions. Jesus remains central — one of history's brightest lights — but he's part of a larger ongoing story."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Latter-day Saints: Divine Son, Expanded Scripture", body: "In the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints (LDS), Jesus is the divine Son of God, the promised Messiah, and the savior of the world. They take the Bible seriously but also believe in additional scripture — the Book of Mormon presents Jesus appearing to people in the ancient Americas after his resurrection.\n\nTheir view of God differs from mainstream Christianity. The Father, the Son, and the Holy Ghost are three distinct beings perfectly united in purpose (the Godhead), rather than one God in three persons (the Trinity). Jesus is understood as pre-existent — he lived with the Father before being born on earth.\n\nSalvation strongly emphasizes Jesus's atoning work, focusing on both Gethsemane and the cross, followed by literal bodily resurrection. They also teach ongoing restoration of divine authority through modern prophets.\n\nJesus isn't peripheral — he's the absolute center. But the framework around him (God's nature, additional scripture, restoration) creates a distinct branch of the Christian family tree.\n\nJEHOVAH'S WITNESSES: THE CREATED SON\n\nJehovah's Witnesses place Jesus at the center of God's plan but understand his identity differently. Jesus is the Son of God, the Messiah, and the world's redeemer — but not God Almighty. Jehovah alone is the one true God, and Jesus is Jehovah's first and greatest creation.\n\nThey point to verses emphasizing Jesus's dependence on the Father: \"The Father is greater than I\" (John 14:28). Many identify Jesus's pre-human existence with Michael the Archangel.\n\nThe crucifixion matters deeply — described as death on a torture stake rather than a traditional cross. Jesus's sacrifice is a ransom making eternal life possible. They teach Jesus was resurrected as a powerful spirit creature, not in a human body of flesh.\n\nA distinctive part: They teach Christ began ruling invisibly as king in heaven in 1914 and that we are living in the last days. Their door-to-door preaching flows from that urgency.\n\nThey honor Jesus, follow him, and trust his sacrifice — but reserve worship exclusively for Jehovah.\n\nPATTERN: Even within Christianity, views of Jesus diverge dramatically. The Trinity isn't universally accepted. The nature of resurrection is debated. Additional scriptures create different narratives. Same starting point (the Gospels), multiple conclusions."),
                ],
                reflectionPrompt: "If groups that all claim to follow Jesus reach different conclusions about who he IS — what does that tell me about the reliability of any single interpretation?"
            ),
            
            // ═══════════════════════════════════════
