            // ═══════════════════════════════════════
            AwakeningLesson(
                id: "ld_m1_l5",
                number: 5,
                title: "New Age View & The Meta-Pattern",
                subtitle: "Christ consciousness and what all 8 views reveal together",
                emoji: "🌀",
                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "New Age: Enlightened Master & Christ Consciousness", body: "New Age spirituality isn't one organized religion — it's a wide umbrella blending self-help, mysticism, metaphysics, and elements of many traditions. The view of Jesus varies, but patterns recur.\n\nMany describe Jesus as an enlightened master — someone who reached a high spiritual state and came to model what humans can become. Phrases like \"ascended master,\" \"way-shower,\" or \"teacher of unconditional love\" are common.\n\nInstead of focusing on Jesus dying for sin and rising again as the center of salvation history, New Age thought often treats those events as symbols: death representing ego death, resurrection representing spiritual awakening.\n\nThe key concept: Christ consciousness — the belief that \"the Christ\" is a universal spiritual energy or state of awareness, not uniquely tied to Jesus alone. Jesus embodied it clearly, but the goal is for YOU to awaken to that same inner divinity.\n\nThis differs sharply from how Jesus presents himself in the Gospels. The New Testament portrays him as someone who speaks with God's authority, calls for repentance, and claims a unique role. New Age readings soften those exclusive claims and reframe them as metaphorical or misinterpreted.\n\nThe center of gravity shifts: In Christianity, the spotlight stays on WHO Jesus is and what he did. In New Age spirituality, it shifts to what Jesus can teach you about your own inner potential. Less courtroom and covenant, more journey and awakening."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "The Meta-Pattern: What All 8 Views Reveal", body: "Now step back and look at ALL eight views together. What pattern emerges?\n\nWHAT THEY ALL SHARE:\n• Universal respect for Jesus's ethical teachings (love, compassion, justice)\n• Recognition of his historical significance\n• Acknowledgment that his life and message changed the world\n\nWHERE THEY DIVERGE:\n• Is he God? (Christianity yes, Islam/Judaism/JW no, others vary)\n• Is he the ONLY way? (Christianity often yes, Hinduism/Bahá'í/Buddhism no)\n• Did he physically die and rise? (Christianity yes, Islam no, JW spiritual only, Bahá'í spiritual)\n• Is his role unique or exemplary? (Christianity unique, New Age exemplary)\n\nTHE DEEPER PATTERN:\nEvery tradition takes the same historical data (a first-century Jewish teacher who was executed and whose followers claimed resurrection) and processes it through a completely different interpretive framework.\n\nJudaism: Doesn't meet messianic criteria.\nIslam: Great prophet, but not final, not divine.\nBuddhism: Admirable but not necessary.\nHinduism: One of many valid paths.\nBahá'í: One in a series of progressive revelations.\nLDS: Divine, with expanded scripture.\nJW: Created son, not God himself.\nNew Age: Symbol of universal consciousness.\nChristianity: God incarnate, unique savior.\n\nNine different conclusions from the same starting point.\n\nWhat does this tell you? That the LENS matters as much as the data. That inherited frameworks shape perception before conscious analysis begins. That the same reality looks completely different depending on which floor you're standing on.\n\nThis is exactly what the Planes of Existence module showed you — same building, different floor, different view. This is what ERSS teaches — every narrative is processed through existing priors.\n\nThe person who has studied ALL views? They can choose their position consciously rather than inheriting it unconsciously. They can hold respect for multiple perspectives without collapsing into relativism OR fundamentalism.\n\nThat's seeing clearly. That's knowing both sides."),
                ],
                reflectionPrompt: "After seeing all 8 views — has my own view of Jesus shifted, deepened, or been confirmed? What does my reaction tell me about my own framework?"
            ),
